        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8ca7c91c-b33f-5991-884a-8ab39a2ddd0d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Platforms: Ford CD2 platform, Mazda GF platform\n- Products: Mazda Capella, Ford Escape, Mazda Tribute, Mercury Mariner, Mercury Villager, Nissan Quest\n- Places: Ohio Assembly\n\nFacts:\n- The Mazda Capella was a mid-size car manufactured by Mazda from 1970 to 2002.\n- Ohio Assembly produced the Mercury Villager and Nissan Quest from 1993 through 2002.\n- The Ford CD2 platform design was based on Mazda's GF platform, which was used by the Mazda Capella/626.\n- The Ford Escape and Mazda Tribute shared underpinnings built from the Ford CD2 platform, which was based on Mazda GF underpinnings.\n- The Ford Escape and Mazda Tribute shared only the roof and floor pressings as common body panels.\n- Ohio Assembly produced the Ford Escape and Mercury Mariner until 2005.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c953b69b-fe11-5d4e-a56e-716a055ef129",
        "text": "Page: Ford CD2 platform. Sentence: The design is based on Mazda's GF platform, used by the Mazda Capella/626.\nPage: Mazda Capella. Sentence: The Mazda Capella is a mid-size car that was manufactured by Mazda from 1970 to 2002.\nPage: Ford Escape. Sentence: Although the Escape and Tribute share the same underpinnings constructed from the Ford CD2 platform (based on Mazda GF underpinnings), the only panels common to the two vehicles are the roof and floor pressings.\nPage: Ohio Assembly. Sentence: It produced the Mercury Villager and Nissan Quest from 1993 through 2002, and the Ford Escape and Mercury Mariner until 2005.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
